"""rbx.py — the Roblox asset kit for Blender. Same API headless (production) and via Blender MCP (iterating).

AUTHOR IN ROBLOX SPACE: studs, Y is up, -Z is the FRONT, +X is the right side.
rot=(rx, ry, rz) is in degrees and means exactly CFrame.Angles(math.rad(rx), math.rad(ry), math.rad(rz)).
The kit converts to Blender space, bakes every material into one texture set, exports FBX, validates,
renders a 2x2 preview sheet and prints one JSON verdict line. You never touch bpy.ops for the basics.

    import rbx
    a = rbx.Asset("crate")                              # wipes the scene, sets up outputs
    a.material("wood", color=(0.45, 0.3, 0.18), rough=0.8, wear=0.3)
    a.material("metal", color=(0.5, 0.5, 0.52), metal=0.9, rough=0.35)
    a.box("Body", size=(4, 4, 4), pos=(0, 2, 0), mat="wood", bevel=0.1)
    with a.frame(pos=(0, 4, 0), rot=(0, 45, 0)):        # children are placed relative to this frame
        a.cylinder("Bolt", radius=0.2, length=0.3, pos=(1.5, 0, 0), mat="metal", axis="Y")
    a.build()                                           # bake -> export -> validate -> preview -> verdict

Outputs (git-ignored): build/models/<name>[_<group>].fbx,
build/models/textures/<name>[_<group>]_{color,rough,metal}.png, build/models/<name>.blend,
build/models/<name>.manifest.json, build/renders/<name>.png (2x2 sheet: front-left, back-right, top, right side).
"""

